          "path": "_m/s/p/3/e/columbus-monument-barcelona-wp/barcelona-47934011408.jpg",
          "filename": "Barcelona (47934011408).jpg",
          "caption": "At the seaward end of the famous street \"La Rambla\" in Barcelona, Spain you come to this column, which dates from 1888.\nIt's the Columbus Monument, a 60 m (197 ft) tall monument to the famous explorer.\nIt's possible to go up inside the narrow column in a small lift for views from the top.\nWhen I say a small lift it really is. Only three people can get in at once and one of them is the operator! When you get out, near the top there is a narrow circular viewing platform which slopes slightly downward on the outside. All in all, an unnerving experience and certainly not for the claustrophobic!\n\nThe other tower which can be seen in the distance is for a cable car that runs from the port to the hill of Montjuic and gives great views over the city.",
          "alt": "At the seaward end of the famous street \"La Rambla\" in Barcelona, Spain you come to this column, which dates from 1888.\nIt's the Columbus Monument, a 60 m (197 ft) tall monument to the famous explorer.\nIt's possible to go up inside the narrow column in a small lift for views from the top.\nWhen I say a small lift it really is. Only three people can get in at once and one of them is the operator! When you get out, near the top there is a narrow circular viewing platform which slopes slightly downward on the outside. All in all, an unnerving experience and certainly not for the claustrophobic!\n\nThe other tower which can be seen in the distance is for a cable car that runs from the port to the hill of Montjuic and gives great views over the city.",
